<?jelly escape-by-default='true'?>
<j:jelly xmlns:j="jelly:core" xmlns:f="/lib/form">
  <f:section title="Build Change Investigator — Slack">
    <f:block>
      Slack delivery discloses investigation summaries outside Jenkins. Channel members may not have Jenkins Item.READ.
      Approve only jobs and folders whose summaries may be shared with the selected channel.
      Store the bot token in Jenkins Credentials as secret text; this configuration stores only its ID.
    </f:block>
    <f:entry title="Enable Slack investigation delivery" field="enabled"><f:checkbox default="false"/></f:entry>
    <f:entry title="Approved destinations" field="destinations">
      <f:repeatableProperty field="destinations" minimum="0" add="Add approved Slack destination"/>
    </f:entry>
    <f:entry title="Saved destination ID to validate"><f:textbox name="destinationId"/></f:entry>
    <f:entry><f:validateButton title="Test Connection" progress="Validating..." method="testConnection" with="destinationId"/></f:entry>
    <f:block>Save first. Test Connection uses auth.test and conversations.info without posting any message. Matching workspace, channel membership and bot identity are required. Slack channel posting restrictions can still prevent delivery.</f:block>
    <f:entry title="Delivery status"><div>${descriptor.deliveryStatus}</div><a href="${rootURL}/bci-slack-delivery/">Review delivery status</a></f:entry>
    <f:entry><f:validateButton title="Re-arm delivery for this controller boot" progress="Approving..." method="rearmDelivery" with=""/></f:entry>
    <f:block>Review this controller and its pending work before re-arming after a restart or restore. An uncertain delivery outcome requires manual reconciliation; it is never automatically resent.</f:block>
  </f:section>
</j:jelly>
